    {
      "stem": "haftarah_after_blessings",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/after",
      "title": {
        "he": "ברכות אחרונות להפטרה",
        "en": "Blessings after the Haphtorah"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s183",
                "printed_page": "80",
                "text": "Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, King of the World, Rock of all eternity, just in all generations, faithful God who says and acts, speaks and fulfils, for all His words are truth and righteousness."
              }
            ],
            "end_reference": true,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/after/tzur"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 2,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s183",
                "printed_page": "80",
                "text": "Faithful art Thou, O Lord our God and faithful are Thy words and not one of Thy words turns back empty; for Thou art a faithful and compassionate God and King. Blessed art Thou, O Lord God who is faithful in all His words."
              }
            ],
            "end_reference": true,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/after/neeman"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 3,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s183",
                "printed_page": "80",
                "text": "Have mercy upon Zion, it is the centre of our life; and save her, whose soul is afflicted, speedily in our days. Blessed art Thou, O Lord, who makes Zion rejoice with her children."
              }
            ],
            "end_reference": true,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/after/rachem"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 4,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s183",
                "printed_page": "80",
                "text": "Let us rejoice, O Lord our God, with the prophet Elijah Thy servant and with the realm of the House of David thine anointed. Speedily may he come that our heart may have joy. Let no stranger sit on his throne, and let others no longer inherit his glory for by Thy Holy Name hast Thou sworn to him that his light shall not be extinguished for ever. Blessed art Thou, O Lord, shield of David."
              }
            ],
            "end_reference": true,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/after/sammechenu"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
